me>Grol</surname><given-names>RPTM</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Tacken MAJB</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The Dutch National Information Network of General Practice (LINH) and quality-of-care data</article-title><source>Quality of preventive performance in general practice: The use of routinely collected data [thesis]</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Nijmegen, Radboud University Nijmegen</publisher-name><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>44</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lamberts</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>ICPC: International classification of primary care</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Oxford, Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Timmermans</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Baselier</surname><given-names>PJAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Winkens</surname><given-names>RAG</given-names></name><name><surname>Arets</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiersma</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>NHG-Standaard Urineweginfecties: Eerste herziening [Guideline of the Dutch College of General Practitioners on urinary tract infections: first revision]</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Utrecht, Nederlands Huisartsen Genootschap (NHG)</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van de Lisdonk</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Verstraeten</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kinderen met urineweginfecties: Verwijzen of niet? Een retrospect